<details class="docs-disclosure"><summary>Which ID do I use?</summary><div class="docs-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Identity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Placement and access</td><td>Project ID and optional real folder ID</td></tr><tr><td>Shot or review item</td><td>Asset ID and assigned production code</td></tr><tr><td>Exact media, prompt or reference</td><td>Version ID</td></tr><tr><td>Production pick</td><td>Asset’s current-version relationship</td></tr><tr><td>Delivery</td><td>Explicit grant and immutable source asset/version tuple</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Metadata saves use revision checks. Upsert changes-feed results by ID because items near a cursor can repeat. That feed reports specific merged/misfiled removals, not every deletion.</p></details>
<details class="docs-disclosure"><summary>Scope, locked folders and operational access</summary><p>A series integration uses a project-scoped credential. Upload permission is not publication permission. Locked folders belong to the creating credential, not any owner browser session. Never log bearer keys or signed media URLs.</p><p>Setup-specific deployment and recovery belong in <a href={resolve('/docs/operations')}>owner operations</a>. The API guide and OpenAPI contract above own request details; this page does not duplicate them.</p></details>
